# Crypto Quant Framework - Cursor Rules

## Project Identity
Multi-Asset Crypto Portfolio (BTC, ETH, SOL, LINK)  
Goal: Alpha with Low Beta | Current: CAGR 57.06%, Beta 0.183

## Architecture
4-phase pipeline: Data → Risk → Strategy → Portfolio  
Risk Engine: Dynamic regime (risk_on/risk_off overlay)

## Current Phase: Block 4
- Stress testing (2018, 2022)
- Multi-factor OLS (Alpha/Beta decomposition)
- Next: Walk-Forward Analysis

## Tech Stack
- Data Handling: Pandas (Current), Plan to migrate to Polars/DuckDB later
- Backtest: VectorBT
- Stats: Statsmodels, SciPy
- Reporting: Pyfolio Reloaded

## Code Standards (MANDATORY)
- Type hints on ALL functions
- OOP architecture (core/, runners/)
- Pytest for every module
- Google-style docstrings
- Log returns (NOT simple returns)

## Anti-Overfitting
1. Walk-Forward (rolling 6mo)
2. T-Test on out-of-sample Sharpe (p < 0.05)
3. VaR/CVaR on stress periods
4. Zero data leakage (non-overlapping features)

## Communication Style
User is direct, technical, zero bullshit.  
Expected from Sonnet:
- Show code immediately when asked
- NO basic explanations (user knows Python/Quant)
- DO highlight trade-offs when multiple options exist
- Ask ONLY essential clarifications (max 1-2 questions)

## Philosophy (Kantian Framework)
Raw data ≠ Reality → Models impose structure on chaos  
Backtesting = Critique of Pure Experience

